    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f4eba559_55a2f5c4",
        "filename": "aarch64/src/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 318,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T05:05:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry for being vague. My point is that this `host_access` bit makes sense for Gunyah, which is going to have a separate memory region for the shared memory, but it will be inaccurate for pKVM, which does not have a separate region for the shared memory.\n\nI need to add a config option to control whether it gets split out. In the case where it isn\u0027t split out (for pKVM), then even when `protection_type.isolates_memory() \u003d\u003d true`, will want `host_access \u003d true`.",
      "parentUuid": "cfe8f195_21ef00eb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 316,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 318,
        "endChar": 94
      },
      "revId": "897a758931505be142ef35b28a2525290091787d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0e5af304_b7420d9f",
        "filename": "aarch64/src/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 318,
      "author": {
        "id": 1858345
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T17:44:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I think I got the idea. The changes in https://r.android.com/2275106 to add a separate memory region will be under some config condition.\n\nI\u0027m not sure if you meant it will come under as some `--flag` option. If so, IMO, this is more of a hypervisor decision rather than user `--flag`.",
      "parentUuid": "f4eba559_55a2f5c4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 316,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 318,
        "endChar": 94
      },
      "revId": "897a758931505be142ef35b28a2525290091787d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d37fe403_f315ef3a",
        "filename": "aarch64/src/lib.rs",
